# The point of #3264, against the SAME fixture `step_over_a_call` uses
# with `stepi`. Read the two transcripts side by side: four `stepi over`s
# to cross line 7, one `step over`. That contrast is the whole feature,
# and keeping both goldens on one story is what makes it legible.
break story.ink:7
run
expect-line 7
step over
expect-line 8
locals
expect-local who = "vendor"
# `next` is GDB's spelling of `step over` — same verb, and the transcript
# shows it resolving to the same thing rather than a second mechanism.
next
expect-line 9
